Sampling validation programs
============================

These C++ programs sample points from spheres, spherical shells, disks, and
cylinders and evaluate Debye scattering kernels sin(q*r)/(q*r).

DebyeSampler.hpp accumulates sampled scattering curves; GenerateSamples.hpp
supplies geometric point generators. Sample_*.cpp are the standalone drivers.
Their behavior is unchanged from their original Mathematica/Sampled location.

The four Tests/Sample_*_test.cpp wrappers include these drivers, compile them
with TESTING enabled, and run through CTest. See Tests/README.md.

To build standalone drivers from the repository root:

    make -C Tests/sampling

Standalone runs use large sample counts. Run an executable from a separate
working directory: its generated curve folders are written to that directory.
Existing reference curves are preserved in Tests/data/sampling/; they are not
automatically regenerated by building the programs.

The associated Mathematica notebooks/PDFs are in docs/derivations/mathematica/.
